From 272da79276365c4da55c38855b4b8e2465ccdbf8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:53:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the Study Timer's fullscreen room and the control that
 would not pause

The fullscreen room painted a tall white island. `.is-fullscreen .card` set
display:none, but `.is-fullscreen .focus-stage` set display:grid later at equal
specificity and won, so the card that *is* the stage came back as a 900px white
slab while the caption, progress bar and task field stayed hidden. The same
cascade hid Pause: the only remaining control was a `{ once: true }` click on
the clock, which allowed one pause and never a resume.

- exempt the stage from the hide rule, paint the room on the fullscreen element
  itself (native fullscreen renders nothing else), and keep the controls on
  screen, dimmed until hover or focus
- put the *stage* fullscreen, not the workspace, so Today's focus, the week
  chart and the session list do not travel into the room
- add a CSS-only immersive fallback for browsers without an Element Fullscreen
  API, with Escape to leave and a page scroll lock
- stop rebuilding the screen on start/pause: `ctx.refresh()` destroyed the
  fullscreen class and every listener in it. The primary control and Finish are
  repainted in place, and the immersive state survives a repaint
- resolve click actions at click time instead of binding per button, so the
  swapped start/pause control keeps working after the markup changes

Verified in headless Chromium: native and fallback paths both cover the
viewport, the clock is centred, controls stay reachable, Escape exits, and
start -> pause -> resume cycles. Night/rain/woodland rooms all paint. 32 timer
tests pass; check.mjs stays at 1,188 checks with the same 7 pre-existing
bundled-bank problems and the suite at 452/27 with no new failures.
